The low pass filters (LPF) are single filters with relay bypasses. Each filter is constructed on the same size cards as the standard modules. There is only one input socket on one edge of the card and an output socket on the opposite edge. The first LPF 
after the }{\f5\uldb Output module}{\v\f5 Output_Module}{\f5  connects to the output pin of that module. This results in the filter output being on the opposite side to that of the Output module after the first LPF. The second LPF is mounted wit
h its input socket connected to the output pin if the first LPF. Each LPF is mounted 180 degrees out from the previous LPF. A total of 5 LPFs are required to cover all HF amateur bands. A given LPF is selected by applying +12 Volts to  its bypass relay. 

